.TH HIDDIFY-TUI 1 "August 2026" "hiddify-tui" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hiddify-tui \- terminal and command-line client for Hiddify Core
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hiddify-tui
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B hiddify-tui
.RI [ options ] command " " [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hiddify-tui
controls a local Hiddify Core gRPC service and stores profiles client-side.
With no command in an interactive terminal it opens the dashboard. Closing the
dashboard does not disconnect an active connection.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR --address " " ADDRESS
Core gRPC address. The default is 127.0.0.1:17078.
.TP
.BR --profile-file " " FILE
Override the client profile store.
.TP
.BR --core-binary " " FILE
Use a specific standalone hiddify-core binary.
.TP
.BR --timeout " " DURATION
Core startup or request timeout.
.TP
.B --json
Produce stable JSON output where supported.
.TP
.B --no-color
Disable terminal color.
.TP
.B --version
Print the client version.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status [--watch]
Show one status snapshot or follow status changes.
.TP
.B connect [--profile ID]
Connect the active or selected profile.
.TP
.B disconnect
Disconnect without stopping the core control service.
.TP
.B restart
Restart using the active profile.
.TP
.B profile
List, show, add, import, rename, activate, refresh, or delete profiles.
.TP
.B outbound
List, select, or test outbounds.
.TP
.B logs [--level LEVEL]
Follow core logs.
.TP
.B settings set FILE
Apply Hiddify settings from JSON.
.TP
.B settings validate FILE
Validate Hiddify settings JSON.
.TP
.B migrate gui
Read and optionally import profiles from the Hiddify GUI database.
.TP
.B install-core
Install the supported standalone core for the current user.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/hiddify/profiles.json
Default client profile store on Linux when XDG_DATA_HOME is unset.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 indicates success, 2 invalid usage, 3 unavailable core, and 4 a rejected operation.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR hiddify-core (1)
